    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule as a read-time derived field, following the project's existing pattern for computed owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` property (readOnly string, enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `membershipTier(Owner)` helper that returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nThe tier is computed from the already-persisted `namesakeCount` (set by `AssignNamesakeCount` at create time) and the owner's `email`, so no entity/DB column was needed \u2014 it's derived when the owner is serialized, exactly matching the `POST` then `GET` flow the acceptance tests exercise.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`), and the entire existing suite remains green.",
